# base.pkgs — what every Ember image has, on every architecture.
#
# Void's own base-system pulls a kernel and firmware, which the Pi profiles
# replace with their own; base-minimal plus the pieces named here is the
# smallest thing that still boots, logs in and reaches a network.
base-minimal
runit-void
dhcpcd
iproute2
iputils
wpa_supplicant
openssh
ca-certificates
util-linux
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
# ⚠ sudo is BASE, not a desktop extra. The image creates a wheel user and drops
# a rule into /etc/sudoers.d — and that directory belongs to the sudo package,
# so without it the image build fails on "No such file or directory" and a
# machine that did build would have an administrative user who cannot administer
# anything. A sudoers rule for an uninstalled package is not a small mistake.
# growpart, for expanding the root partition on first boot after the image has
# been written to a card larger than itself. It is built for growing a MOUNTED
# partition, which is what the running root is.
cloud-guest-utils
sudo
nano
less
which
xbps
